sections.wikitext:
[[File:Ray Parker Jr., 1984.jpg|thumb|Parker on "Ghostbusters": "I was the last resort. I really didn't think I could do it."<ref>{{Cite news |last=Hunt |first=Dennis |date=1984-08-19 |title=Ray Parker Jr. Going Like Ghostbusters |pages=72 (Calendar section) |work=Los Angeles Times |url=https://www.newspapers.com/image/400671223/?terms=ray%20parker%20jr&match=1}}</ref>]]
The music video for the song was directed by [[Ivan Reitman]], who also directed the ''Ghostbusters'' film, and produced by Jeffrey Abelson. It features a young woman played by actress [[Alan_F._Horn#Personal_life|Cindy Harrell]]<ref>{{cite web |last=Ryan |first=Mike |date=June 6, 2014 |title=Who Ya Gonna Call? The Inside Story Of The 'Ghostbusters' Music Video |url=https://screencrush.com/ghostbusters-music-video/ |website=[[ScreenCrush]]}}</ref> who is haunted by a [[ghost]] portrayed by Parker, roaming a nearly all-black house interior (with vibrant neon designs outlining the sparse architectural and industrial features) until the woman finally calls the service.{{citation needed|date=March 2021}}

Directed by Reitman, the "Ghostbusters" music video was No. 1 on [[MTV]] and features cameos from [[Chevy Chase]], [[Irene Cara]], [[John Candy]], [[Melissa Gilbert]], [[Ollie E. Brown]], [[Jeffrey Tambor]], [[George Wendt]], [[Al Franken]], [[Danny DeVito]], [[Carly Simon]], [[Peter Falk]] and [[Teri Garr]]. None were paid for participating but did so as a favor to Reitman.<ref name="AFI" /><ref name="CBCJul16"/><ref name="MediumJul16"/>

The video concludes with Parker and the stars of the film, in full Ghostbuster costume, dancing down the streets of [[New York City]]. [[Times Square]] was closed in order to film the scene, although a sizable crowd may still be seen in the background.<ref name=":0" /> The Ghostbusters also perform the same dance in the closing credits to ''[[The Real Ghostbusters]]'', the cartoon spin-off, as well as in a trailer for ''[[Ghostbusters: The Video Game]]'' (2009).{{citation needed|date=March 2021}}

