Over the years, a handful of local and national businesses across North America and around the world have done parodies of the Ghostbusters theme for advertising or promotional purposes, and used an instrumental version of either the original theme or a remake. The most notable parodies were used by [[CBS]] station [[KMOV|KMOX-TV]] (now KMOV) in St. Louis, [[AutoNation]], and the Carpet Mart chain of [[Central Pennsylvania|Central]], [[Berks County, Pennsylvania|Berks County]], and [[Lehigh Valley]] [[Pennsylvania]] among others.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qRHw0XyyZnk|title=KMOV "Channel 4 Newsbusters" Promo|date=September 13, 2008|via=YouTube}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pYJjsTf68CY|title=Autonation|date=September 10, 2013|via=YouTube}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Y0iyWS7sgmw|title=Carpet Mart Commercial|date=August 4, 2008|via=YouTube}}</ref> 

In the [[United Kingdom|UK]], the [[118 118 (UK)|118 118]] directory assistance telephone service also used the Ghostbusters theme in one of their ads, and featured Ray Parker Jr. performing the parody.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=edIWsAQduRA|title=118 118 Uk  Ghostbusters parody with Ray Parker Jr|date=February 7, 2009|via=YouTube}}</ref> In Romania, [[Automobile Dacia]] released a [[television advertisement]] in 2018 for one of its models, the [[Dacia Duster|Duster]], accompanied by the song, in an instrumental version, but with people in various costumes singing "Go, Duster!" when in the standard song the chorus says "Ghostbusters!".<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WNHvizqMLTM|title=Publicité 2018 - Dacia - Duster  - Go Duster - Homme en Pyjama|date=September 17, 2018|via=YouTube}}</ref>{{better source needed|date=July 2026}}

American musician and comedian [[Neil Cicierega]] uses the song in "[[Bustin (song)|Bustin]]", released on his 2017 [[mashup (music)|mashup]] album ''[[Mouth Moods]]''.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Heins|first=Scott|title=Flashback Friday: Ray Parker Jr's "Ghostbusters" Is Reborn As The Brilliant "Bustin"|url=https://www.okayplayer.com/news/ray-parker-jr-bustin.html|access-date=March 6, 2021|website=okayplayer|date=25 September 2015}}</ref>{{better source needed|date=July 2026}}

